# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Transient gating-candidate checkpoints (TrainingManager.py writes these
# under Networks/ mid-episode and always deletes them afterward - see
# _candidate_tmp.keras / _gating_candidate.keras - but ignore them anyway
# in case a run gets killed mid-gating and leaves one behind).
Networks/_candidate_tmp.keras
Networks/_gating_candidate.keras

# Large, regenerable self-play artifacts from past runs. These sit outside
# the paths the code actually reads/writes (Networks/, TrainingExamples/ -
# see CLAUDE.md/ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW.md), and individual files here run
# into the hundreds of MB - past GitHub's 100MB per-file limit, so they
# couldn't be pushed as plain git objects even if tracked.
self_play_Networks/
self_play_TrainingExamples/
PretrainExamples/

# Network.keras (current champion), Networks/ (promoted checkpoints), and
# TrainingExamples/ (replay buffer) are intentionally NOT ignored - these
# are what Project.py resumes from, so they need to travel to the Windows
# desktop for training to continue rather than restart.
